          "title": "Multiplicative Real Inverse and Flux Conservation",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== Multiplicative Real Inverse and Flux Conservation\nFor any non-zero real aperture parameter \\( x \\in \\mathbb { R } \\setminus \\{ 0 \\} \\), the multiplicative inverse \\( x ^ { - 1 } \\) represents the reciprocal aperture flux scaling that satisfies: \\[ x \\cdot x ^ { - 1 } = 1 \\quad \\implies \\quad \\left ( \\lim _ { N \\to \\infty } r _ N \\right ) \\cdot \\left ( \\lim _ { N \\to \\infty } r _ N ^ { - 1 } \\right ) = \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\]\n\n\nThis guarantees strict conservation of light flux and geometric scale invariance across all real transformations within the Counting-Iris Number System.\n\n[#chap-the-multiscale-resolution-numbers]"
