          "title": "Basis Vectors of \\( Cl ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\)",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== Basis Vectors of \\( Cl ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\)\n\nThe basis vectors spanning the Clifford space \\( Cl ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\) are given by: \\[ \\{ e _ 1 , e _ 2 , e _ 3 , e _ 4 , e _ + , e _ - \\} \\]\n\n\nsatisfying the metric signatures: \\[ e _ 1 ^ 2 = e _ 2 ^ 2 = e _ 3 ^ 2 = 1 \\qquad e _ 4 ^ 2 = 0 \\qquad e _ + ^ 2 = 1 \\qquad e _ - ^ 2 = - 1 \\]\n\n\nThe conformal null basis vectors \\( e _ \\infty \\) and \\( e _ 0 \\) are defined as: \\[ e _ \\infty = e _ + + e _ - \\qquad e _ 0 = \\frac { 1 } { 2 } ( e _ - - e _ + ) \\]\n\n\nwhich satisfy the properties: \\[ e _ \\infty ^ 2 = e _ 0 ^ 2 = 0 \\qquad e _ 0 \\cdot e _ \\infty = - 1 \\]\n\n\n[#definition-master-field-equation]\n[DEFINITION]\n.Definition: The Master Field Equation\n====\nIn the Clifford algebra \\( Cl ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\), the **Master Field Equation** is defined as: \\[ D F _ { \\text { total } } = J _ { \\text { total } } \\]\n\n\nwhere the differential operator \\( D \\) and convective time derivative \\( D _ t \\) are given by: \\[ D = \\nabla + e _ 4 \\frac { 1 } { c } D _ t \\qquad D _ t = \\frac { \\partial } { \\partial t } - u \\cdot \\nabla \\]\n\n\nthe total electromagnetic field \\( F _ { \\text { total } } \\) is a multivector combining electric vector and magnetic trivector flux: \\[ F _ { \\text { total } } = E e _ 4 + c B ( e _ 1 \\wedge e _ 2 \\wedge e _ 3 ) \\]\n\n\nand the total source current density \\( J _ { \\text { total } } \\) and velocity multivector \\( U \\) are given by: \\[ J _ { \\text { total } } = \\rho _ 0 U \\qquad U = u + c e _ 4 \\]\n===="
