          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== Proof of the MSRA Ring Homomorphism\n\n[#theorem-msra-homomorphism]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Ring Homomorphism Property of Main Scale Projection\n====\nThe Main Scale Projection operator \\( ( \\downarrow ) : \\text { Fin } ( \\mathbb { R } ^ { \\ast } ) \\to \\mathbb { R } \\) is a strict ring homomorphism mapping finite multiscale vernier quantities onto standard real flux values, preserving addition and multiplication: \\[ ( \\downarrow ) ( x ^ { \\ast } + y ^ { \\ast } ) = ( \\downarrow ) ( x ^ { \\ast } ) + ( \\downarrow ) ( y ^ { \\ast } ) , \\qquad ( \\downarrow ) ( x ^ { \\ast } \\cdot y ^ { \\ast } ) = ( \\downarrow ) ( x ^ { \\ast } ) \\cdot ( \\downarrow ) ( y ^ { \\ast } ) \\]\n\n\n*Proof:*\n. Represent finite vernier quantities in canonical decomposition: \\( x ^ { \\ast } = x + \\epsilon _ x ^ { \\ast } \\) and \\( y ^ { \\ast } = y + \\epsilon _ y ^ { \\ast } \\), where \\( x , y \\in \\mathbb { R } \\) are main-scale real parts and \\( \\epsilon _ x ^ { \\ast } , \\epsilon _ y ^ { \\ast } \\in \\text { Fin } ( \\mathbb { R } ^ { \\ast } ) \\) are vernier residuals satisfying \\( ( \\downarrow ) ( \\epsilon _ x ^ { \\ast } ) = 0 \\) and \\( ( \\downarrow ) ( \\epsilon _ y ^ { \\ast } ) = 0 \\).\n\n. **Additive Preservation**: \\[ x ^ { \\ast } + y ^ { \\ast } = ( x + y ) + ( \\epsilon _ x ^ { \\ast } + \\epsilon _ y ^ { \\ast } ) \\implies ( \\downarrow ) ( x ^ { \\ast } + y ^ { \\ast } ) = x + y + ( \\downarrow ) ( \\epsilon _ x ^ { \\ast } + \\epsilon _ y ^ { \\ast } ) = x + y + 0 = ( \\downarrow ) ( x ^ { \\ast } ) + ( \\downarrow ) ( y ^ { \\ast } ) \\]\n\n\n. **Multiplicative Preservation**: \\[ x ^ { \\ast } \\cdot y ^ { \\ast } = ( x + \\epsilon _ x ^ { \\ast } ) ( y + \\epsilon _ y ^ { \\ast } ) = x y + x \\epsilon _ y ^ { \\ast } + y \\epsilon _ x ^ { \\ast } + \\epsilon _ x ^ { \\ast } \\epsilon _ y ^ { \\ast } \\]\n\nApplying \\( ( \\downarrow ) \\) to each term yields \\( ( \\downarrow ) ( x y ) = x y \\), \\( ( \\downarrow ) ( x \\epsilon _ y ^ { \\ast } ) = x \\cdot 0 = 0 \\), \\( ( \\downarrow ) ( y \\epsilon _ x ^ { \\ast } ) = y \\cdot 0 = 0 \\), and \\( ( \\downarrow ) ( \\epsilon _ x ^ { \\ast } \\epsilon _ y ^ { \\ast } ) = 0 \\cdot 0 = 0 \\). Thus: \\[ ( \\downarrow ) ( x ^ { \\ast } \\cdot y ^ { \\ast } ) = x y = ( \\downarrow ) ( x ^ { \\ast } ) \\cdot ( \\downarrow ) ( y ^ { \\ast } ) \\]\n\nThis proves that \\( ( \\downarrow ) \\) is a complete ring homomorphism from \\( \\text { Fin } ( \\mathbb { R } ^ { \\ast } ) \\) to \\( \\mathbb { R } \\). \\( \\square \\)\n===="
