          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== The MSRA Vernier Measure Uniformity Theorem\n\n[#theorem-msra-measure-uniformity]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Constructive MSRA Vernier Measure Additivity\n====\nFor any finite disjoint collection of discrete measurement intervals \\( \\mathcal { U } _ 1 , \\mathcal { U } _ 2 , \\dots , \\mathcal { U } _ k \\subset \\mathcal { G } _ N \\), the vernier aperture flux measure \\( \\mu _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\) satisfies strict finite additivity and Main Scale invariant convergence under grid refinement.\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Vernier Flux Measure Definition**: Define the aperture flux measure of a finite discrete set \\( \\mathcal { U } \\subset \\mathcal { G } _ N \\) as \\( \\mu _ { \\mathcal { I } } ( \\mathcal { U } ) = \\sum _ { r \\in \\mathcal { U } } \\delta \\cdot \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\), where \\( \\delta = 1 / N \\) is the fundamental aperture step size.\n\n. **Disjoint Partition Count**: Let \\( \\mathcal { U } _ i \\cap \\mathcal { U } _ j = \\emptyset \\) for \\( i \\neq j \\). The operational count of elements satisfies \\( | \\bigcup _ { i = 1 } ^ k \\mathcal { U } _ i | = \\sum _ { i = 1 } ^ k | \\mathcal { U } _ i | \\).\n\n. **Scale-Invariant Evaluation**: Evaluating the flux sum yields: \\[ \\mu _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\left ( \\bigcup _ { i = 1 } ^ k \\mathcal { U } _ i \\right ) = \\sum _ { r \\in \\bigcup \\mathcal { U } _ i } \\delta = \\sum _ { i = 1 } ^ k \\left ( \\sum _ { r \\in \\mathcal { U } _ i } \\delta \\right ) = \\sum _ { i = 1 } ^ k \\mu _ { \\mathcal { I } } ( \\mathcal { U } _ i ) \\]\n\n\n. **Main Scale Invariance**: Applying Main Scale Projection \\( ( \\downarrow ) \\) removes higher-order vernier residual boundary terms, ensuring that \\( ( \\downarrow ) \\mu _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\) matches the standard length measure on rational sub-intervals.\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: Measure additivity holds strictly for all finite operational measurement sets on \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\). \\( \\square \\)\n===="
