          "id": "sec-the-discrete-sobolev-aperture-norm-equivalence-theorem",
          "title": "The Discrete Sobolev Aperture Norm Equivalence Theorem",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== The Discrete Sobolev Aperture Norm Equivalence Theorem\n\n[#theorem-sobolev-iris-equivalence]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Finite Sobolev Aperture Equivalence in Cl(4,1,1)\n====\nOn discrete grid \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\), the MSRA vernier derivative norm \\( \\| D _ { \\mathcal { I } } f \\| _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\) is bounded by multivector aperture norms, establishing exact finite Sobolev-type bounds without continuous completions.\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Vernier Difference Operator**: Define the MSRA vernier derivative \\( D _ { \\mathcal { I } } f ( r ) = \\frac { f ( r + \\delta ) - f ( r ) } { \\delta } \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\).\n\n. **Aperture Energy Bound**: Expand \\( D _ { \\mathcal { I } } f ( r ) \\) in terms of the Fourier-Iris basis coefficients \\( c _ k \\): \\[ D _ { \\mathcal { I } } f ( r ) = \\sum _ { k = 0 } ^ { N - 1 } c _ k \\frac { \\iota ^ { k \\delta N } - 1 } { \\delta } \\iota ^ { k r N } \\]\n\n\n. **Metric Norm Evaluation**: Taking the Iris metric norm yields \\( \\| D _ { \\mathcal { I } } f \\| _ { \\mathcal { I } } ^ 2 \\le C _ N \\sum _ { k = 0 } ^ { N - 1 } k ^ 2 | c _ k | ^ 2 \\), where \\( C _ N \\) is a finite rational constant dependent on grid resolution \\( N \\).\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: The discrete Sobolev norm \\( \\| f \\| _ { H ^ 1 _ { \\mathcal { I } } } = \\| f \\| _ { \\mathcal { I } } + \\| D _ { \\mathcal { I } } f \\| _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\) is well-defined and strictly finite for all discrete aperture fields on \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\). \\( \\square \\)\n====\n\n[#chap-applications-to-probability-theory]"
