          "title": "The Jaynesian Information Conservation Law",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== The Jaynesian Information Conservation Law\n\n[#theorem-entropy-conservation]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Entropy Conservation in Closed Aperture Systems\n====\nUnder unitary multivector gauge transformations in \\( Cl ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\), the total Jaynesian information entropy \\( S _ { \\text { MaxEnt } } ( P ) = - \\sum _ { r \\in \\mathcal { G } _ N } P ( r ) \\ln P ( r ) \\) of an aperture probability state remains invariant.\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Unitary Gauge Action**: Let \\( U \\in Spin ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\) be a multivector gauge transformation satisfying \\( U \\bar { U } = \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\).\n\n. **State Density Transformation**: The transformed probability density satisfies \\( P' ( r ) = P ( U r \\bar { U } ) \\).\n\n. **Sum Invariance**: Since unitary transformations preserve grid measure \\( \\mu _ { \\mathcal { I } } ( U \\mathcal { U } \\bar { U } ) = \\mu _ { \\mathcal { I } } ( \\mathcal { U } ) \\), the entropy sum satisfies: \\[ S _ { \\text { MaxEnt } } ( P' ) = - \\sum _ { r \\in \\mathcal { G } _ N } P ( U r \\bar { U } ) \\ln P ( U r \\bar { U } ) = - \\sum _ { r' \\in \\mathcal { G } _ N } P ( r' ) \\ln P ( r' ) = S _ { \\text { MaxEnt } } ( P ) \\]\n\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: Jaynesian information entropy is strictly conserved under gauge field evolutions in \\( Cl ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\). \\( \\square \\)\n====\n\n[#chap-applications-to-constructive-statistics]"
