          "id": "sec-the-finite-sample-cramer-rao-aperture-inequality",
          "title": "The Finite-Sample Cramer-Rao Aperture Inequality",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== The Finite-Sample Cramer-Rao Aperture Inequality\n\n[#theorem-cramer-rao-aperture]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Finite-Sample Vernier Variance Lower Bound\n====\nThe variance of any unbiased operational estimator \\( T ( X ) \\) for parameter \\( \\theta \\) on discrete grid \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\) satisfies: \\[ \\text { Var } _ { \\mathcal { I } } ( T ( X ) ) \\ge \\frac { 1 } { I _ { \\mathcal { I } } ( \\theta ) } \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\]\n\nwhere \\( I _ { \\mathcal { I } } ( \\theta ) \\) is the Fisher aperture information multivector norm.\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Unbiased Expectation Condition**: Let \\( \\mathbb { E } _ { \\text { MaxEnt } } [ T ( X ) ] = \\theta \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\). Differentiating both sides with respect to \\( \\theta \\) using MSRA derivative \\( D _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\) yields: \\[ \\sum _ { x \\in \\mathcal { G } _ N } T ( x ) D _ { \\mathcal { I } } P ( x \\mid \\theta ) = \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\]\n\n\n. **Score Operator Identity**: Rewrite \\( D _ { \\mathcal { I } } P ( x \\mid \\theta ) = P ( x \\mid \\theta ) D _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\ln P ( x \\mid \\theta ) \\).\n\n. **Cauchy-Schwarz Multivector Inequality**: Applying the Iris inner product inequality to \\( ( T ( X ) - \\theta \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } ) \\) and \\( D _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\ln P ( X \\mid \\theta ) \\) gives: \\[ \\mathbb { E } \\left [ ( T ( X ) - \\theta \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } ) ^ 2 \\right ] \\cdot \\mathbb { E } \\left [ ( D _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\ln P ( X \\mid \\theta ) ) ^ 2 \\right ] \\ge \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\]\n\n\n. **Fisher Information Identification**: Recognizing \\( I _ { \\mathcal { I } } ( \\theta ) = \\mathbb { E } \\left [ ( D _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\ln P ( X \\mid \\theta ) ) ^ 2 \\right ] \\) yields the exact lower bound \\( \\text { Var } _ { \\mathcal { I } } ( T ( X ) ) \\ge I _ { \\mathcal { I } } ( \\theta ) ^ { - 1 } \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\).\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: No unbiased operational estimator on \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\) can exceed the precision bound imposed by the Fisher aperture information norm. \\( \\square \\)\n====\n\n[#chap-applications-to-conventional-statistics]"
