          "id": "sec-fundamental-theorem-of-constructive-rational-algebra",
          "title": "Fundamental Theorem of Constructive Rational Algebra",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== Fundamental Theorem of Constructive Rational Algebra\n\n[#theorem-fundamental-theorem-rational-algebra]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Fundamental Theorem of Constructive Rational Algebra\n====\nEvery non-constant monic polynomial \\( P ( z ) = \\sum _ { k = 0 } ^ m a _ k z ^ k \\) with rational multivector coefficients in \\( Cl ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\) admits a finite rational root decomposition on a finite rational grid extension \\( \\mathcal { G } _ { N ' } \\), decomposing uniquely into linear factors \\( P ( z ) = \\prod _ { j = 1 } ^ m ( z - \\lambda _ j ) \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\) without appealing to an uncountably infinite field closure.\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Finite Vernier Grid Search**: On finite resolution grid \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\), evaluate the scalar magnitude \\( \\| P ( z ) \\| _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\). Since \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\) is a finite discrete set, the minimum \\( \\min _ { z \\in \\mathcal { G } _ N } \\| P ( z ) \\| _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\) is attained at a finite grid point \\( \\lambda _ 1 \\).\n\n. **Grid Refinement Iteration**: If \\( \\| P ( \\lambda _ 1 ) \\| _ { \\mathcal { I } } > 0 \\), refine grid resolution to \\( N ' = N \\cdot M \\). In a finite number of rational refinement steps, \\( P ( \\lambda _ 1 ) = 0 \\).\n\n. **Polynomial Division**: Dividing \\( P ( z ) \\) by \\( ( z - \\lambda _ 1 ) \\) yields quotient polynomial \\( Q ( z ) \\) of degree \\( m - 1 \\). Inductive reduction terminates in exactly \\( m \\) finite steps. \\( \\square \\)\n===="
