          "id": "sec-fundamental-structure-theorem-of-finite-boolean-lattices",
          "title": "Fundamental Structure Theorem of Finite Boolean Lattices",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== Fundamental Structure Theorem of Finite Boolean Lattices\n\n[#theorem-boolean-power-set-isomorphism]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Fundamental Structure Theorem of Finite Boolean Lattices\n====\nLet \\( B \\) be a finite Boolean lattice (a bounded distributive complemented lattice). Let \\( \\text{Atoms} ( B ) = \\{ p \\in B \\setminus \\{ \\mathbf { 0 } _ B \\} \\mid \\forall x \\in B , \\mathbf { 0 } _ B \\le x \\le p \\implies ( x = \\mathbf { 0 } _ B \\lor x = p ) \\} \\). Then \\( B \\) is isomorphic to the power set lattice \\( \\mathcal { P } ( \\text{Atoms} ( B ) ) \\) under set union and intersection. In particular, \\( | B | = 2 ^ k \\) where \\( k = | \\text{Atoms} ( B ) | \\).\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Atomic Representation**: In a finite Boolean algebra, every element \\( a \\in B \\) is uniquely expressible as the join of all atoms beneath it: \\( a = \\bigvee \\{ p \\in \\text{Atoms} ( B ) \\mid p \\le a \\} \\).\n\n. **Boolean Isomorphism**: The assignment \\( \\psi ( a ) = \\{ p \\in \\text{Atoms} ( B ) \\mid p \\le a \\} \\) defines a bijection from \\( B \\) to \\( \\mathcal { P } ( \\text{Atoms} ( B ) ) \\) preserving meets, joins, and complements.\n\n. **Cardinality**: Since \\( \\mathcal { P } ( X ) \\) for a finite set of size \\( k \\) has size \\( 2 ^ k \\), \\( | B | = 2 ^ k \\). \\( \\square \\)\n====\n\n[#references-boolean-structure]"
